('getter',(B,184),row('QrSymbol.Size returns Modules.GetLength(0),the first dimension of the private matrix produced by EncodeQr. EncodeQr allocates square size=17+4*QR version and strips QRCoder quiet zone;Size therefore excludes quiet modules and is used by TotalDots and StampQr index bounds. Getter does not cache dimensions or validate null/rectangular matrices,which current sole construction path excludes. Array contents remain mutable despite record property init-only.', 'Existing QrSymbol.Modules bool[,] reference.', 'Integer first dimension;null matrix throws NullReferenceException if future internal caller violates construction invariant.', 'No writes/allocation/external effect.', 'Private renderer data,not JSON DTO or authenticated input directly;QR payload already processed by EncodeQr.', 'No database access.', 'Bounds mx/my versus Size assume square matrix;current EncodeQr creates square,so no present rectangular out-of-bounds demonstrated.', 'Constant-time array length,called repeatedly per raster module;no benchmark run.', 'No second dimension check;copy of record shares same matrix and getter reflects its fixed dimensions.', ['Future null/rectangular constructor use would invalidate stamp assumptions;not currently reachable'], ['Pure null/rectangular internal fixture and maximum QR version dimensions;no physical printing'], ['BitmapTicketRenderer.cs184 Size','EncodeQr200-229 creates square','TotalDots186','StampQr537-550'])),
('getter',(B,186),row('QrSymbol.TotalDots adds two QrQuietModules borders to Size then multiplies integer ModuleDots. Quiet modules constant4 and validated EncodeQr module size determine physical pixel square. RenderSegment uses this value for measured height and centered placement;StampQr uses same value loop bounds,so layout and raster agree. Getter makes no readability/width decision itself;EncodeQr rejects symbols that cannot fit content width.', 'Size getter,ModuleDots init-only int,QrQuietModules4.', 'Integer full square side including quiet border.', 'Pure calculation,no allocation or state change.', 'Private QrSymbol constructor can accept arbitrary ModuleDots but actual EncodeQr enforces >=3 and fit;do not pretend getter validates external input.', 'No SQL/persistence.', 'Quiet-zone inclusion must happen once:upstream QRCoder border is stripped;this getter adds it back in printer dots.', 'Constant arithmetic;unchecked int multiplication theoretical overflow only with invalid future internal values.', 'Measured height and stamp use same function;record with-copy shares Modules but copies ModuleDots scalar.', ['No current overflow/zero module path established through EncodeQr'], ['Quiet-border exactly4modules each side,fit threshold and minimum-size QR;no printer execution'], ['BitmapTicketRenderer.cs186','EncodeQr200-229','RenderSegment274-275,374','StampQr537-550'])),
('getter',('src/Falah.PrintAgent/Transports.cs',21),row('NetworkTicketTransport.Description interpolates configured host and port as network host:port. It is read for startup/attempt logs and reported error context,not used to establish a connection;SendAsync separately uses those fields. Getting it cannot prove reachability,bytes accepted or physical paper. IPv6 hosts are unbracketed in description and potentially ambiguous but actual socket call uses original host string.', '_host string and _port int set by constructor.', 'Fresh diagnostic string.', 'String allocation only,no TCP attempt.', 'Configuration-to-log/server error boundary exposes printer network address;no credentials or PIN field used.', 'Getter no DB;processor error may later persist string in print result.', 'Diagnostic route identification,not print state.', 'O(host length) string allocation per logging read.', 'No identity/parser contract;two differently formatted configs may log similarly.', ['Unbracketed IPv6 diagnostic ambiguity;not socket parsing defect'], ['Host/port exact output and no socket side effect;IPv6 diagnostics'], ['Transports.cs14-21 constructor/getter','SendAsync23-32','PrintJobProcessor.cs111,121'])),
('getter',('src/Falah.PrintAgent/Transports.cs',49),row('SerialTicketTransport.Description returns serial portName@baudRate from constructor fields. Getter performs no COM enumeration/open/flush and does not verify speed matches hardware;those actions occur only in SendAsync. It is logged for both success and failure,so a diagnostic string is not evidence a serial printer acknowledged output.', '_portName and _baudRate immutable fields.', 'Fresh serial diagnostic string.', 'Allocation only,no serial device operation.', 'Local serial configuration exposed to operator/server error log;no auth secret.', 'No DB read/write in getter.', 'Distinguishes configured serial destination/speed from physical print proof.', 'Constant fields/string formatting,no hardware wait.', 'No status/retry/idempotency semantics;same getter value across multiple attempts.', ['Successful transport label cannot distinguish buffer flush from paper'], ['PortName/baud formatting including odd configured names;getter no COM open'], ['Transports.cs42-49','SendAsync51-64','PrintJobProcessor.cs111,121'])),
('getter',('src/Falah.PrintAgent/Transports.cs',80),row('FileTicketTransport.Description explicitly includes file directory and no physical printing suffix. This is safety-relevant messaging consumed by processor logs;it does not perform write or create directory. Constructor already creates directory separately,while SendAsync writes timestamped escpos file. Getter therefore must remain distinguishable from hardware success and cannot be read as printer availability.', '_directory constructor field.', 'file <directory> (no physical printing) diagnostic.', 'Only string allocation;Directory.CreateDirectory belongs constructor,not getter.', 'Local output path can enter server print error/logs;no file content or secret read.', 'No DB operation.', 'Explicit verification-only transport marker counters claiming successful file output means physical receipt.', 'Linear string length,no disk I/O here.', 'No unique attempt/file path exposed by getter;all same-directory attempts share description.', ['Directory path disclosure in broad print detail read remains prior boundary concern'], ['Suffix retained for paths with spaces,relative/absolute paths;no write from getter'], ['Transports.cs74-80','SendAsync82-86','PrintJobProcessor.cs111,121'])),
('getter',('src/Falah.PrintAgent/WindowsSpoolerTicketTransport.cs',27),row('WindowsSpoolerTicketTransport.Description wraps configured queue name in quotes with RAW annotation. No Win32 OpenPrinter/GetPrinter call occurs;getter can return for nonexistent queue. RAW states selected transport datatype,not verified driver capability or completed physical output. Processor reports transport description after Send returns,retaining PRT002 spooler-accepted versus paper distinction.', '_printerName set by constructor.', 'windows printer "name" (RAW) diagnostic.', 'String allocation,no spooler/native call.', 'Configured queue names flow to logs and server error detail;getter performs no escaping beyond quotes.', 'No SQL in getter.', 'Device label and intended datatype only;no completion acknowledgement.', 'No blocking call,unlike Send synchronous Win32 path.', 'Quoted names may contain quotes/newlines;not executable shell string in this getter.', ['Log formatting for unusual names;no command execution path from interpolation established'], ['Missing queue still description,embedded quotes,RAW marker,no physical job'], ['WindowsSpoolerTicketTransport.cs25-32','Send38+','PrintJobProcessor.cs111,121'])),
('getter',('src/Falah.Application/Reports/DailyStatementDtos.cs',79),row('DailyEmployeeRowDto.TotalPaidTodayPiastres sums AdvancePaidToday,WithdrawalPaidToday,PayrollSettlementPaidToday and standalone SettlementPaidToday;it excludes accrued wages/overtime/bonus,deductions and all-time RunningBalance. Producer BuildEmployeeRows groups day ledger and sums four distinct debit types,so normal source rows do not double-count kinds. Standalone Settlement default0 preserves older constructor payloads. This getter is presentation arithmetic,not permission,payout or balance guard.', 'Four long daily debit totals from DTO constructor;last Settlement defaults0.', 'long total daily payouts;unchecked addition can overflow adversarial/extreme supplied values.', 'Pure arithmetic,may be serialized/read by WinUI binding;no payment action.', 'Server producer supplies ledger-derived data,but public record constructor/JSON can hold inconsistent or negative fields without validation.', 'No SQL in getter;DailyStatementQueryService155-184 is actual day ledger producer.', 'DailyStatementView293 displays total;must not call it earned pay or remaining balance. Existing test196 asserts standalone3000 included.', 'Constant four additions;not a bottleneck.', 'Copies update fields shallow/value scalars;derived getter recomputes after with-copy. No cached total that could drift separately.', ['Boundary long overflow not validated here;financial command invariant belongs upstream'], ['Four distinct nonzero types,default missing Settlement,negative/extreme totals and serialization;existing test read,not executed'], ['DailyStatementDtos.cs70-80','DailyStatementQueryService.cs155-184','DailyStatementView.xaml293','DailyStatementVerticalSliceTests.cs180-197'])),
('generated',(B,177),row('Measured is a private positional record holding TicketElement,Height,optional Font,optional mutable CellFonts list,ContentWidth and optional QrSymbol. Generated constructor/init properties preserve supplied references;record equality/list equality is reference-based for Font/list/element objects rather than deep raster equality,and with-copy would share disposable resources. Actual RenderSegment creates per-element records then disposes Font and CellFonts after drawing;no observed with/equality use,so generated copy cannot be assumed safe resource ownership API. Generated ToString could describe record fields but is not used as ticket content.', 'Element/Height/Font?/CellFonts?/ContentWidth/Qr? from RenderSegment measurement cases.', 'Measurement descriptor;compiler-generated value members not individually counted.', 'Construction stores references;record itself not IDisposable and performs no disposal.', 'Private trusted renderer context,not HTTP DTO;ticket data carries user text but Font allocation internal.', 'No DB.', 'DrawPill/DrawRow consume measured font/height;resource lifetime controlled by RenderSegment cleanup,not generated behavior.', 'One record allocation per ticket element plus lists/fonts;shallow equality is no substitute for visual comparison.', 'Generated copies share Font/list;current no copy observed. Cleanup not in finally for all exceptional drawing paths remains original renderer concern.', ['Do not introduce with-copy as independent disposable ownership without design'], ['Exception during draw/resource disposal and copy-sharing pure tests;no physical print'], ['BitmapTicketRenderer.cs177-178','RenderSegment258-395','DrawPill400','DrawRow424'])),
('generated',(B,182),row('QrSymbol positional record stores mutable bool[,] Modules reference and ModuleDots scalar with init properties. Generated constructor does not enforce square/nonempty/non-null matrix or positive dot size;EncodeQr sole observed construction path supplies square matrix and validated size. Generated equality compares array reference,not contents;ToString does not serialize pixel matrix,so neither equality nor string is raster identity. A with-copy shares underlying matrix;getters Size/TotalDots are separately reviewed executable facets.', 'Modules bool[,],ModuleDots int.', 'Private QR rendering metadata,not wire contract.', 'Reference assignment/allocation only;no raster or printer operation from generated members.', 'Internal QR encoder result;not directly deserialized externally.', 'No SQL.', 'StampQr uses bounds/module quiet-zone;mutating shared matrix would change both record copies rendering.', 'Array memory dominates record;no deep equality/hash traversal of pixels.', 'Identical matrices independently allocated compare unequal;shared array mutation not reflected as new record identity.', ['Equality must not be used as rendered-content cache key without deep digest'], ['Square/rectangular/null fixture,shared with-copy mutation,independent equal-content arrays;current path remains validated'], ['BitmapTicketRenderer.cs182-187','EncodeQr200-229','StampQr537-550'])),
('generated',(B,190),row('QrPlacement is a private positional record of Symbol reference and integer Left/Top. Generated constructor/copy carries reference and coordinates without clipping;StampQr clips each target x/y against raster dimensions before writing. Equality delegates Symbol record equality,which remains matrix-reference based,so equal-looking codes are not necessarily equal placements. No generated member acknowledges print or writes pixels;placement is created in RenderSegment for later QR stamping.', 'QrSymbol,int Left,int Top.', 'Placement value descriptor used by raster stage.', 'Allocation only;no bitmap mutation until StampQr called.', 'Private renderer math from contentWidth/y,not user-supplied JSON coordinates.', 'No persistence.', 'Bounds clipping counters out-of-paper pixel writes;negative placement truncates symbol rather than validation error.', 'Small allocation per QR;StampQr cost proportional TotalDots squared belongs explicit method.', 'with-copy shares Symbol/matrix;coordinates copied as values. No observed placement equality/dedupe logic.', ['Clipping can produce unreadable cropped QR if upstream positioning invariant changes'], ['Negative/offedge placements,symbol quiet zone and shallow equality;software bitmap fixture only'], ['BitmapTicketRenderer.cs190','RenderSegment374','StampQr537-550'])),
('generated',('src/Falah.PrintAgent/UnreportedAttemptStore.cs',27),row('StoredAttempt positional record is the durable JSON journal value:AttemptRequestId,Succeeded,Error?,AtUtc. Constructor/with-copy do not validate nonblank id/timestamp or establish hardware success. System.Text.Json roundtrips public generated properties;Find returns immutable scalar/string record so no exposed mutable collection. Processor writes false uncertain state before transport,then actual transport result;restart reuses same AttemptRequestId for report rather than printing again. Generated ToString contains Error diagnostic and timestamp,so should not be treated sanitized telemetry automatically.', 'AttemptRequestId string,Succeeded bool,Error nullable string,AtUtc DateTimeOffset.', 'Journal serialization/deserialization record,not paper completion proof.', 'Record allocation itself noneexternal;Remember/Save persist entire dictionary separately.', 'File deserialization trusts journal contents after JSONshape;malformed JSON fails closed but semantically malformed record fields not constructor-validated.', 'No SQL in record;report result later writes server attempt.', 'Succeeded means transport-returned status,PRT002,not physical output;uncertain false entries deliberately stop replay print.', 'Small record,whole journal serialization cost belongs Save;no generated observable notifications.', 'Value equality exact strings/scalars;with changes can alter report identity,actual processor preserves it. Journal key is PrintJobId separate from record.', ['Manual journal tampering/semantic corruption not detected by record constructor;local trust issue'], ['Missing/null AttemptRequestId,uncertain false/error roundtrip,same record across restart and no duplicate physical output;no hardware executed'], ['UnreportedAttemptStore.cs27,46-87','PrintJobProcessor.cs80-100,104-127,131-161']))
